('b72fb343-b03b-566b-9122-79d100287bf3','1e12cc1f-87cb-54c7-9c78-b7ca57a32612',7,'measurement','اندازه گیری','spoken & written','a number or amount shown on a measuring instrument','[ countable ]',null,'یک عدد یا مقدار نشان داده شده بر روی یک ابزار اندازه گیری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We take temperature readings every two hours.","translation":"ما هر دو ساعت یک بار دما را اندازه گیری می کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604357.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('84ef3430-9664-5d32-a213-1bac42130887','1e12cc1f-87cb-54c7-9c78-b7ca57a32612',8,'in parliament','در مجلس','spoken & written','one of the occasions in the British Parliament or the US Congress when a suggested new law is discussed','[ countable ]',null,'یکی از مواقعی که در پارلمان بریتانیا یا کنگره آمریکا درباره قانون جدید پیشنهادی بحث می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the second reading of the Energy Bill","translation":"دومین قرائت لایحه انرژی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00711.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('684d249c-4dca-5571-8317-631696b1412d','d9258319-b581-5044-8588-f93b28cce694',1,null,null,'spoken & written','what actually happens or is true , not what is imagined or thought','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'واقعیت، حقیقت؛ واقعیت (زندگی)؛ واقعیت (تلفیقی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the harsh/grim/stark reality (= conditions that are really very bad ) We want to protect our children from the harsh reality of our violent world.','political/social/economic realities He''s ignoring political realities.','face reality (= accept it ) It''s painful, but you have to face reality.','confront a reality (= consider or deal with it ) They had to confront some unpleasant realities about themselves.','ignore a reality They are ignoring the reality of Arab politics.','wake up to reality (= realize what is happening or real ) Well, they need to wake up to reality.','lose touch with reality (= no longer know about ordinary things or what is possible ) If all you have is the show-business world, you kind of lose touch with reality.','escape from reality The programmes help viewers escape from reality.','bring somebody back to reality (= make them realize what is happening around them or true ) She was brought back to reality by the pain in her ankle.','become a reality (= really happen, after being hoped for, feared, etc by someone ) Last June, her longed-for baby finally became a reality.','reflect reality (= match or show what is really happening or true ) Do these novels accurately reflect contemporary reality?','bear no relation to reality (= not match what is really happening or true ) His vision of European politics bears no relation to reality.','be divorced from reality (= not connected in any way to what is really happening ) His ideas are completely divorced from reality.','a dose of reality (= an experience of what things are really like ) I got my first dose of reality when I reported to work at my new job.','somebody''s grasp of reality (= their understanding of reality ) They portrayed her as a sick woman with only a tenuous grasp of reality.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the distinction between fantasy and reality","translation":"تمایز بین خیال و واقعیت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000483702.mp3"},{"sentence":"TV is used as an escape from reality .","translation":"تلویزیون به عنوان فرار از واقعیت استفاده می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000483703.mp3"},{"sentence":"I think the government has lost touch with reality (= no longer understands what is real or true ) .","translation":"من فکر می کنم دولت ارتباط خود را با واقعیت از دست داده است (= دیگر نمی فهمد واقعی یا واقعی چیست).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604500.mp3"},{"sentence":"political realities","translation":"واقعیت های سیاسی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001770452.mp3"},{"sentence":"Millions of people live with the harsh realities of unemployment.","translation":"میلیون ها نفر با واقعیت های سخت بیکاری زندگی می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604505.mp3"},{"sentence":"The reality is that young people will not go into teaching until salaries are higher.","translation":"واقعیت این است که جوانان تا زمانی که حقوقشان بیشتر نشود، به سمت تدریس نمی روند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604501.mp3"},{"sentence":"The paperless office may one day become a reality .","translation":"دفتر بدون کاغذ ممکن است روزی به واقعیت تبدیل شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604504.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
